  "transcript": [
    {
      "start": 31.6,
      "end": 46.4,
      "text": "On 275 and 285",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 46.4,
      "end": 48.42,
      "text": "Also in stereo on VHF",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 48.42,
      "end": 50.86,
      "text": "This is National Radio 1",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 50.86,
      "end": 61.76,
      "text": "Well, hello there",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 61.76,
      "end": 63.7,
      "text": "Thomas the Vance here, TV on the radio",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 63.7,
      "end": 66.52,
      "text": "And welcome once again to the Friday Rock Show",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 66.52,
      "end": 68.97,
      "text": "Happy Easter to you",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 68.97,
      "end": 71.39,
      "text": "This evening we have extracted from the archives",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 71.39,
      "end": 74.11,
      "text": "A 1975 session that was recorded by Queen",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 74.11,
      "end": 75.11,
      "text": "And it's a good one",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 75.11,
      "end": 77.31,
      "text": "Also we repeat our session by Saxon",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 77.31,
      "end": 79.07,
      "text": "Who are doing very nicely, thank you very much",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 79.07,
      "end": 80.45,
      "text": "with their album Wheels of Steel.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 81.41,
      "end": 96.84,
      "text": "And we've got new cuts by Black Sabbath, Van Halen, Def Leppard and Gamma.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 97.4,
      "end": 102.34,
      "text": "And classic cuts by Bebop Deluxe, or Deluxe if you like, Led Zeppelin, Rush and Roxy Music.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 102.6,
      "end": 104.6,
      "text": "Not forgetting, of course, our Friday Night Connection.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 104.84,
      "end": 108.06,
      "text": "That time of the week when a little bit of titillation comes under your door.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 109.02,
      "end": 110.8,
      "text": "But this evening we start with Whitesnake.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 110.8,
      "end": 175.0,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 110.8,
      "end": 175.0,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 180.0,
      "end": 535.0,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 180.0,
      "end": 535.0,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 540.0,
      "end": 829.51,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 540.0,
      "end": 829.51,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 829.51,
      "end": 832.19,
      "text": "And that, of course, was Def Leppard from their album On Through the Night,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 832.19,
      "end": 833.39,
      "text": "which is in the charts at the moment.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 833.53,
      "end": 834.65,
      "text": "The track was The Overture.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 837.33,
      "end": 839.79,
      "text": "And I played especially for Geddy George and Angus Slade,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 839.79,
      "end": 842.27,
      "text": "and also the clan of McGregors and Trendy Briggy",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 842.27,
      "end": 845.81,
      "text": "and all the def leopard freaks who live in and around Pocklington in York.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 847.92,
      "end": 849.92,
      "text": "And before that, you heard something by Whitesnake",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 849.92,
      "end": 851.98,
      "text": "that's going to be issued as a single quite shortly.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 852.26,
      "end": 853.66,
      "text": "It's called Fool for Your Love.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 854.24,
      "end": 859.62,
      "text": "It's 13 minutes after 10 o'clock.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 859.74,
      "end": 863.82,
      "text": "Now let's replete, I'm sorry, or in a row, just repeat it.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 864.18,
      "end": 867.26,
      "text": "This is Saxon, and it really is nice to know that we played this.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 867.72,
      "end": 869.38,
      "text": "We were the first people ever to do this session,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 869.48,
      "end": 871.64,
      "text": "and we played it just about two months ago.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 871.8,
      "end": 873.56,
      "text": "And we're going to repeat the whole session, all five tracks.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 873.6,
      "end": 874.64,
      "text": "I'm sure you recognize this.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 874.94,
      "end": 876.02,
      "text": "It's Motorcycle Man.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 876.02,
      "end": 878.05,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 876.02,
      "end": 878.05,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 879.45,
      "end": 880.77,
      "text": "Well, it will be when he revs up.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 883.05,
      "end": 887.85,
      "text": "That was Made in Heaven by Bebop Deluxe,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 887.85,
      "end": 1256.59,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 887.85,
      "end": 1256.59,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 1256.59,
      "end": 1258.29,
      "text": "and I played it specially for all the lower sixths",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1258.29,
      "end": 1261.05,
      "text": "at Woodhouse Grove School from T.A. Ledgard,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1261.17,
      "end": 1263.97,
      "text": "who lives in Bradford, which is BD-10-1,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1264.25,
      "end": 1266.19,
      "text": "or O-N-R, I think it is, actually.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1267.18,
      "end": 1269.26,
      "text": "Something that T.A. says in his letter is,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1269.44,
      "end": 1271.86,
      "text": "do I know anything about Mr. Nelson at the moment?",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1271.96,
      "end": 1274.42,
      "text": "Well, the last I heard was that he, at the moment,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1274.5,
      "end": 1275.96,
      "text": "does not have a record deal,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1276.12,
      "end": 1277.68,
      "text": "but he does have a completed album.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1277.68,
      "end": 1282.86,
      "text": "So what's going to happen in the future, I guess, is that he'll get a record deal and then put out the album.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1283.66,
      "end": 1287.54,
      "text": "Also played for Kevin Davis of [redacted address] in Grantham in Lynx,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1287.66,
      "end": 1290.84,
      "text": "and for the whole of the heavy metal stronghold in Ancaster in Lynx.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1291.46,
      "end": 1297.62,
      "text": "And for Joe O'Riordan and all his mates at, I think it's the St. Iliot's College in Cardiff.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1298.3,
      "end": 1302.22,
      "text": "And before that, you heard Motorcycle Man by Saxon from our session by them.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1303.08,
      "end": 1308.76,
      "text": "And here's Led Zeppelin.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1308.76,
      "end": 1313.56,
      "text": "was Black Sabbath with their new lead singer",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1440.0,
      "end": 1795.0,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 1440.0,
      "end": 1795.0,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 1800.0,
      "end": 1979.76,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 1800.0,
      "end": 1979.76,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 1979.76,
      "end": 1981.64,
      "text": "Ronnie Dio, ex of course of Rainbow",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1981.64,
      "end": 1983.24,
      "text": "a track from their album Heaven and Hell",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1983.24,
      "end": 1985.0,
      "text": "the track was called Children of the Sea",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1985.0,
      "end": 1987.92,
      "text": "and before that Led Zeppelin and All My Love",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1987.92,
      "end": 1989.86,
      "text": "and that was specially for a lady by the name of Dawn",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1989.86,
      "end": 1992.2,
      "text": "who was 19 on February the 28th of March",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1992.2,
      "end": 1994.12,
      "text": "with lots and lots of love from Mike Woods",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1994.12,
      "end": 1995.76,
      "text": "and it was also for everybody",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1995.76,
      "end": 1997.7,
      "text": "at the South East Essex Sixth Form College",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1997.7,
      "end": 1999.64,
      "text": "especially Sue and Lorraine and Arlette and Julia",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1999.64,
      "end": 2001.86,
      "text": "and Jackie and Jackie and Carol and Basil and Simon",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2001.86,
      "end": 2003.86,
      "text": "and Sybil and Andy and Mark and Darren",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2003.86,
      "end": 2005.14,
      "text": "and Martin and Andy and Steve",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2005.14,
      "end": 2007.08,
      "text": "and wish them all the best of luck brother",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2007.08,
      "end": 2009.0,
      "text": "with the Ray Levels, with best wishes from",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2009.0,
      "end": 2010.5,
      "text": "Jackie Gall of Benfleet in Essex.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2011.08,
      "end": 2013.06,
      "text": "It was also for Wills and Dick and Paul",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2013.06,
      "end": 2014.98,
      "text": "and Butts and Pike, who go to the",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2014.98,
      "end": 2016.96,
      "text": "Bartholomew School in Ensham and Oxford.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2017.12,
      "end": 2018.52,
      "text": "Believe it or not, that's where I was born.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2019.26,
      "end": 2021.02,
      "text": "And also, I have to say hello",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2021.02,
      "end": 2022.94,
      "text": "to Jeff Jebbett and Phil the Radio",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2022.94,
      "end": 2025.08,
      "text": "Blair, and tell them both that",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2025.08,
      "end": 2027.22,
      "text": "they're much loved by a lady whose name",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2027.22,
      "end": 2028.96,
      "text": "is Elaine. She lives in",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2028.96,
      "end": 2039.21,
      "text": "Nottingham and Saxon.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2340.0,
      "end": 2454.95,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 2340.0,
      "end": 2454.95,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 2454.95,
      "end": 2456.51,
      "text": "And that was Rush from their first album,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2456.61,
      "end": 2458.69,
      "text": "and a track called In The Mood, and it was specially for",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2458.69,
      "end": 2460.55,
      "text": "Alec McInnes in Ayrshire",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2460.55,
      "end": 2461.21,
      "text": "in Scotland",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2461.21,
      "end": 2462.39,
      "text": "and for Bevan Winchester",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2462.39,
      "end": 2463.85,
      "text": "Ken in Cheshire",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2463.85,
      "end": 2464.83,
      "text": "with lots and lots",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2464.83,
      "end": 2465.35,
      "text": "of best wishes",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2465.35,
      "end": 2466.17,
      "text": "from Bill Shepard",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2466.17,
      "end": 2466.63,
      "text": "who lives in",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2466.63,
      "end": 2467.21,
      "text": "Astley Bridge",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2467.21,
      "end": 2467.81,
      "text": "in Bolton",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2467.81,
      "end": 2470.14,
      "text": "and also",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2470.14,
      "end": 2470.64,
      "text": "it was for",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2470.64,
      "end": 2471.16,
      "text": "Amp and Boz",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2471.16,
      "end": 2471.62,
      "text": "and Fart",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2471.62,
      "end": 2473.16,
      "text": "who live in",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2473.16,
      "end": 2473.9,
      "text": "Bloxwich",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2473.9,
      "end": 2475.02,
      "text": "near Walsall",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2475.02,
      "end": 2476.62,
      "text": "and we played",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2476.62,
      "end": 2477.2,
      "text": "a rush track",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2477.2,
      "end": 2477.82,
      "text": "for Dave Russell",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2477.82,
      "end": 2478.8,
      "text": "and Simon Ritingale",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2478.8,
      "end": 2479.7,
      "text": "and all the other",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2479.7,
      "end": 2480.12,
      "text": "rush fans",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2480.12,
      "end": 2481.34,
      "text": "at Smesto Comprehensive",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2481.34,
      "end": 2482.36,
      "text": "School in Wolverhampton",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2482.36,
      "end": 2483.38,
      "text": "with very best wishes",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2483.38,
      "end": 2484.24,
      "text": "from Martin Harvey",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2484.24,
      "end": 2485.6,
      "text": "and particularly",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2485.6,
      "end": 2486.52,
      "text": "a rush track",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2486.52,
      "end": 2487.98,
      "text": "for Neil Randall",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2487.98,
      "end": 2489.18,
      "text": "of [redacted address]",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2489.18,
      "end": 2490.46,
      "text": "Stonebroom Derbyshire",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2490.46,
      "end": 2492.48,
      "text": "Cos he's 16 today",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2492.48,
      "end": 2493.48,
      "text": "Happy birthday, Neil",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2493.48,
      "end": 2494.94,
      "text": "Remember to say hi to your mates",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2494.94,
      "end": 2497.08,
      "text": "Phil and Steve and Andy and Dave and Tim and Mac",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2497.08,
      "end": 2502.37,
      "text": "And before that, you heard Strangers in the Night by Saxon",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2502.37,
      "end": 2503.71,
      "text": "I'll do a correction on that",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2503.71,
      "end": 2506.43,
      "text": "The track we actually played was Backs to the Wall by Saxon",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2506.43,
      "end": 2508.67,
      "text": "We've got three more to follow by then",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2508.67,
      "end": 2510.09,
      "text": "And talking about sessions",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2510.09,
      "end": 2513.09,
      "text": "Which we do here, as you well know on the Friday Rock Show",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2513.09,
      "end": 2516.73,
      "text": "We did one this week for Broadcast in the Future by Trespass",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2516.73,
      "end": 2519.05,
      "text": "Who this week are doing three gigs in London",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2519.05,
      "end": 2521.55,
      "text": "and if you'd like to go and see them, just check it out in the music comics.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2526.96,
      "end": 2529.16,
      "text": "Ninety minutes before eleven o'clock it is,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2529.24,
      "end": 2531.52,
      "text": "and now here's some Queen, as recorded,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2531.64,
      "end": 2533.94,
      "text": "not as I said at the beginning of the programme in 1975,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2534.24,
      "end": 2535.96,
      "text": "but actually in 1973.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2536.68,
      "end": 2543.88,
      "text": "And that was Queen, out of the archives in Keep Yourself Alive,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2880.0,
      "end": 3025.24,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 2880.0,
      "end": 3025.24,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 3025.24,
      "end": 3027.32,
      "text": "a song that eventually became, of course, their first single,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3027.42,
      "end": 3029.38,
      "text": "and before that you heard See What A Fool I've Been.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3029.84,
      "end": 3032.68,
      "text": "Queen at the moment are recording a brand new album on and off in Germany",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3032.68,
      "end": 3033.84,
      "text": "for release later this year,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3033.98,
      "end": 3038.3,
      "text": "and they should also be bringing out a Greatest Hits sometime this year.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3038.3,
      "end": 3040.76,
      "text": "More from Queen as the evening progresses.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3048.03,
      "end": 3049.25,
      "text": "Back to Saxon.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3049.67,
      "end": 3056.87,
      "text": "Brand new Van Halen album, which is called Women and Children First.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3420.0,
      "end": 3551.72,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 3420.0,
      "end": 3551.72,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 3551.72,
      "end": 3555.4,
      "text": "The album, or rather the track we played you was called In the Cradle Will Rock.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3555.5,
      "end": 3558.5,
      "text": "And The Cradle, I think, is rocky at the moment over there in Belfast 14.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3558.64,
      "end": 3561.18,
      "text": "The one that has the body of Damien Crudden in it.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3561.26,
      "end": 3562.46,
      "text": "Mr. Crudden, good evening to you.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3562.9,
      "end": 3567.82,
      "text": "Also got to say hello to everybody who goes to the Dalrida Grammar School in Ballymoney in Northern Ireland.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3567.94,
      "end": 3569.54,
      "text": "Particularly all the people in the Lower Six.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3569.54,
      "end": 3572.42,
      "text": "that's Irwin and Willis and Jonathan and Jacko",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3572.42,
      "end": 3574.3,
      "text": "and David and Alistair and Dermot",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3574.3,
      "end": 3575.98,
      "text": "and Mully and also",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3575.98,
      "end": 3578.5,
      "text": "Nigel Boyce who wants his name read out loud",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3578.5,
      "end": 3579.6,
      "text": "Nigel Boyce",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3579.6,
      "end": 3582.86,
      "text": "and particularly Albert Parker and Philip Cook",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3582.86,
      "end": 3584.6,
      "text": "and Andy Crump and Martin Sims",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3584.6,
      "end": 3586.36,
      "text": "and Steve Grindle and Charlie Brown",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3586.36,
      "end": 3588.52,
      "text": "from Simon Porter, good wishes come",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3588.52,
      "end": 3590.94,
      "text": "Simon lives in Evesham near Worcestershire",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3590.94,
      "end": 3594.09,
      "text": "too many Easter eggs",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3594.09,
      "end": 3596.23,
      "text": "today, it's affecting the larynx",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3596.23,
      "end": 3597.53,
      "text": "I think, nonetheless",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3597.53,
      "end": 3599.99,
      "text": "at two minutes before eleven o'clock it's time for the",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3599.99,
      "end": 3600.79,
      "text": "Friday Night Connection.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3600.87,
      "end": 3602.33,
      "text": "Now, the tracks that we played you last week",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3602.33,
      "end": 3603.19,
      "text": "were these,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3603.45,
      "end": 3604.31,
      "text": "Night by Night,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3604.57,
      "end": 3607.09,
      "text": "from the album Pretzel Logic by Steely Dan,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3607.81,
      "end": 3609.37,
      "text": "My Pink Half of the Drainpipe",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3609.37,
      "end": 3611.91,
      "text": "from The Donut in Granny's Greenhouse",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3611.91,
      "end": 3613.31,
      "text": "by the Bonzo Dog Doodah Band,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3613.69,
      "end": 3615.41,
      "text": "and Goodbye Pork Pie Hat",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3615.41,
      "end": 3617.09,
      "text": "from Wired by Jeff Beck.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3618.49,
      "end": 3619.37,
      "text": "Needless to say,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3619.59,
      "end": 3621.15,
      "text": "the answer was",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3621.15,
      "end": 3622.25,
      "text": "things to eat.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3622.43,
      "end": 3623.75,
      "text": "Pretzels and donuts",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3623.75,
      "end": 3624.99,
      "text": "and things to eat.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3625.79,
      "end": 3627.05,
      "text": "Not a lot of people got it right.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3627.29,
      "end": 3628.99,
      "text": "Not a lot of people were probably feeling hungry",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3628.99,
      "end": 3629.95,
      "text": "this time last Friday.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3629.95,
      "end": 3634.97,
      "text": "that philip e lombard of [redacted address] burnley in lancashire got it right didn't you phil",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3634.97,
      "end": 3640.07,
      "text": "and he is going to receive a 10 pound record token for his trouble congratulations philip",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3640.07,
      "end": 3647.6,
      "text": "and as always we've asked the recipient of our 10 pound record token to put together their own",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3647.6,
      "end": 3653.54,
      "text": "friday night connection three pieces of music with a theme or connection here they come see if",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3653.54,
      "end": 3662.54,
      "text": "you can spot them our easter friday night connection three bits of music they have",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4603.69,
      "end": 4611.01,
      "text": "somewhere in them a theme interwoven connection set by philip e lombard of burnley and lancashire",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4611.01,
      "end": 4615.41,
      "text": "If you think you know what the answer is, jot it down on a postcard or any type of communication you like.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4616.02,
      "end": 4625.36,
      "text": "And send it along to Tommy Mance, The Friday Night Connection, The Friday Rock Show, BBC Radio 1, London, W1A4WW.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4626.04,
      "end": 4630.08,
      "text": "But don't forget to put your own Friday Night Connection in there as well.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4630.24,
      "end": 4631.6,
      "text": "Three bits of music with a theme.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4631.6,
      "end": 4632.94,
      "text": "The theme can be anywhere.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4633.44,
      "end": 4639.42,
      "text": "It can be the songs, it can be the album sleeves, literally anywhere that you want it to be.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4639.42,
      "end": 4645.95,
      "text": "Once again, the address is Friday Night Connection, BBC Radio 1, London, W1A, 4WW.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4646.73,
      "end": 4647.27,
      "text": "And good luck.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4647.75,
      "end": 4656.49,
      "text": "It's 11.16, here's Saxon.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4656.49,
      "end": 4663.09,
      "text": "Tigers of Pan tang and their single called Don't Touch Me There.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4663.09,
      "end": 4972.9,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 4663.09,
      "end": 4972.9,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 4972.9,
      "end": 4978.6,
      "text": "And next week on the Friday Rock Show, we will have the first ever BBC Radio 1 session by the Tigers of Pan tang.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4978.78,
      "end": 4981.34,
      "text": "And before that, you heard Saxon from our session.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4981.62,
      "end": 4984.52,
      "text": "And the track we're playing, or rather did play, was Stallions of the Highway,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4984.66,
      "end": 4988.6,
      "text": "which was that single that they brought out that was in the alternative chart for a long, long time.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4988.6,
      "end": 4990.94,
      "text": "Haven't played Roxy music for a long time",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4990.94,
      "end": 4992.24,
      "text": "So let's put that one to rights",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5040.0,
      "end": 5395.0,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 5040.0,
      "end": 5395.0,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 5083.5,
      "end": 5039.7,
      "text": "This track is from an import album.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5400.0,
      "end": 5692.94,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 5400.0,
      "end": 5692.94,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 5692.94,
      "end": 5695.96,
      "text": "It's not a, what do you say, released in this country at the moment.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5696.08,
      "end": 5697.86,
      "text": "It's purely on import on Elektra.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5698.06,
      "end": 5701.0,
      "text": "It's by a band called Gamma, G-A-M-M-A.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5701.06,
      "end": 5702.02,
      "text": "The track's Fight to the Finish,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5702.3,
      "end": 5705.5,
      "text": "and it's the band that's been put together by Ronnie Montrose in the U.S. of A.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5706.0,
      "end": 5706.7,
      "text": "Nice album.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5707.38,
      "end": 5710.28,
      "text": "And before that, something from the album Stranded by Roxy Music.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5710.28,
      "end": 5714.6,
      "text": "It was song for Europe, and I played that because Pete Fern of number 1A,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5714.74,
      "end": 5717.64,
      "text": "Wick Parade, Little Hampton in West Sussex, asked me to.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5717.64,
      "end": 5721.6,
      "text": "wants me to say hello to his girlfriend carol meeks and also to his tuesday night",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5721.6,
      "end": 5730.64,
      "text": "boozing partner from worthing that's pete poland and his wife vicky cheers to all of you here's",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5730.64,
      "end": 5743.84,
      "text": "queen out of the archives as recorded on the 25th of the 7th way back in 1973 a nice set son and",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5760.0,
      "end": 7230.72,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 5760.0,
      "end": 7230.72,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 7229.9,
      "end": 7234.06,
      "text": "that was todd rungren from an american radio broadcast doing a live version of just one",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7234.06,
      "end": 7235.72,
      "text": "Victory, and before that you heard",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7235.72,
      "end": 7238.08,
      "text": "Every Day I Have the Blues by Chuck Berry, and prior to that",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7238.08,
      "end": 7240.24,
      "text": "Saxon and Still Fit to Boogie",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7240.24,
      "end": 7242.06,
      "text": "and they're going to undertake an enormous",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7242.06,
      "end": 7243.54,
      "text": "tour during April and May",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7243.54,
      "end": 7245.86,
      "text": "headlining this time, which is nice to see",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7245.86,
      "end": 7248.18,
      "text": "Hope you enjoyed our archive set by Queen",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7248.18,
      "end": 7250.04,
      "text": "next week, the first ever radio",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7250.04,
      "end": 7252.04,
      "text": "session by the Tigers of Pan tang, and out of the",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7252.04,
      "end": 7256.38,
      "text": "archives, The Nice, and tomorrow",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7256.38,
      "end": 7258.38,
      "text": "between 4 and 7.30 on Rock on Saturday",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7258.38,
      "end": 7259.62,
      "text": "Pete Townsend will be",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7259.62,
      "end": 7262.44,
      "text": "introducing exclusively for Radio",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7262.44,
      "end": 7264.56,
      "text": "One tracks for Rom, his",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7264.56,
      "end": 7270.76,
      "text": "new lp also we've got ub40 girl school and the psychedelic birds and in concert we have",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7270.76,
      "end": 7275.56,
      "text": "nazareth our engineer tonight was phil thank you phil mr tony wilson will now give you a",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7275.56,
      "end": 7283.39,
      "text": "brief appraisal of the program once another week off fine not with the cuts you'll probably get",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7283.39,
      "end": 7288.21,
      "text": "one so will i judging on tonight's performance i'll try and do better tomorrow i hope you enjoyed",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7288.21,
      "end": 7305.98,
      "text": "the music i thought the presenter was dreadful happy easter good night and god bless",
      "source": "TV"
    }
  ]
}